From e1e992f24eff809031a5ad54ac9fe1a598a42357 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: adesh chaudhari <superbhel7@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 7 Aug 2026 08:27:50 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 2/9] feat(frontend): API client layer with auth, envelope
 unwrap and error mapping
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Implements YG-1 — the whole integration hangs off this.

- client.js: axios instance, Bearer token from localStorage on every request,
  and a response interceptor that unwraps the { success, message, data }
  envelope so callers receive data directly (plan 2.2).
- Errors surface as ApiError carrying the server's own message, with 429
  exposed as isRateLimited so callers can back off (plan 2.3).
- auth/events/shows/bookings modules map 1:1 to the frozen contract (plan 3).
- enrich.js is a temporary workaround for SZ-1: BookingResponse has no event
  title/venue/date, so it resolves them via a cached show -> event lookup.
  It self-disables once the DTO carries eventTitle, and the file can then go.

Note for SZ-5: JwtAuthFilter swallows invalid tokens and leaves the request
anonymous, so an expired session arrives as 403, not 401. The interceptor
treats both as a dead session; a clean JSON 401 would let us drop that branch.
